      "value": {
        "body": "A fetch from a client that announced shallow boundaries treated the\nclient's haves as complete history: the send set excluded everything\nreachable from the haves, including ancestors the client does not\nhold. A want that peels to such an ancestor (an annotated tag on an\nolder commit) then produced a pack that failed the client's\nconnectivity check. This broke every GOPROXY=direct go get, since the\ngo tool fetches shallowly first.\n\nRoute client-side shallow boundaries into pack selection and stop the\nhave-closure ascent at them: the client has a shallow commit and its\ntree, but nothing above it. Server grafts already cut the ascent the\nsame way.\n\nFixes #769\n\nSigned-off-by: Mads R. Havmand <mads@v42.dk>",
        "$type": "sh.tangled.repo.pull",
        "title": "knot2: pack objects behind client shallow boundaries",
